.TH GBARE 1 "2025-12-05" "gbare" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gbare \- manage bare Git repositories on remote servers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gbare
.IR command " [" options "] [" arguments "]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gbare
is a zsh plugin for managing bare Git repositories on remote servers (Linux/NAS) via SSH.
It provides a simple command-line interface similar to GitHub's \fBgh\fR CLI for creating,
cloning, listing, and deleting bare repositories on your own server.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR create ", " c " [" name "] [" -y | --yes "]
Create a new bare repository on the remote server.
If \fIname\fR is omitted, uses the current directory name.
The \fB-y\fR or \fB--yes\fR flag skips the confirmation prompt.
Also initializes a local git repository and adds the remote if not already initialized.
.TP
.BR list ", " ls ", " l
List all bare repositories on the remote server.
.TP
.BR clone ", " cl " <" name "> [" directory "]
Clone a repository from the remote server.
If \fIdirectory\fR is specified, clones into that directory.
.TP
.BR delete ", " rm ", " d " <" name ">
Delete a repository from the remote server.
Requires typing the repository name for confirmation.
.TP
.BR info ", " i " <" name ">
Show repository information including server, SSH URL, branches, and tags.
.TP
.BR url ", " u " <" name ">
Print the SSH URL for a repository.
.TP
.BR remote ", " r " [" name "] [" remote "] [" -y | --yes "]
Add a remote to an existing local git repository.
If \fIname\fR is omitted, uses the current directory name.
If \fIremote\fR is omitted, defaults to "origin".
The \fB-y\fR or \fB--yes\fR flag skips the confirmation prompt.
.TP
.BR config ", " cfg
Display the current gbare configuration.
.TP
.BR help ", " h
Show help message with usage information.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -y ", " --yes
Skip confirmation prompts. Available for \fBcreate\fR and \fBremote\fR commands.
.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
.TP
.B GBARE_USER
SSH username for the remote server. Default: \fByumenomatayume\fR
.TP
.B GBARE_HOST
Remote server hostname or IP address. Default: \fBnas\fR
.TP
.B GBARE_PORT
SSH port number. If not set or empty, uses SSH default port 22.
.TP
.B GBARE_PATH
Base path for bare repositories on the remote server.
Default: \fB/volume1/homes/${GBARE_USER}/git\fR
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Create a repository with the current directory name:
.RS
.nf
gbare create
.fi
.RE
.TP
Create a repository without confirmation:
.RS
.nf
gbare create myproject -y
.fi
.RE
.TP
List all repositories:
.RS
.nf
gbare list
.fi
.RE
.TP
Clone a repository:
.RS
.nf
gbare clone myproject
.fi
.RE
.TP
Add a remote to an existing local repository:
.RS
.nf
gbare remote myproject
.fi
.RE
.SH CONFIGURATION
Environment variables can be set in \fB~/.zshrc\fR or via plugin managers like Sheldon.

Example for Sheldon (\fB~/.config/sheldon/plugins.toml\fR):
.RS
.nf
[plugins.gbare-env]
inline = """
export GBARE_USER="your-username"
export GBARE_HOST="your-server"
export GBARE_PATH="/var/git"
"""

[plugins.gbare]
github = "yourusername/gbare"
apply = ["source"]
.fi
.RE
.SH REQUIREMENTS
.TP
.B zsh
Shell environment
.TP
.B git
Version control system
.TP
.B ssh
SSH client for remote server access
.SH TROUBLESHOOTING
.TP
.B SSH connection errors
Verify SSH connectivity: \fBssh user@your-server "echo 'Connection OK'"\fR
.TP
.B Repository not found
Check configuration: \fBgbare config\fR
.TP
.B Non-standard SSH port
Set \fBGBARE_PORT\fR environment variable (e.g., \fBexport GBARE_PORT="2222"\fR)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1),
.BR ssh (1),
.BR git-init (1)
